# Upstream patch for github.com/cloudflare/azul — Ed25519 chain signatures in x509_util
#
# WHY: azul's x509_util::is_link_valid dispatches on the signature OID and
# accepts ECDSA P-256/384/521 and RSA PKCS#1 v1.5 only. Ed25519 (RFC 8410,
# id-Ed25519 1.3.101.112) falls to `_ => false`, so a Static CT log built on
# ct_worker refuses every Ed25519-signed chain at add-chain. notme's root and
# all its issued certificates are Ed25519, and Ed25519 is a first-class
# WebPKI signature algorithm (RFC 8410; CA/B Forum permits it).
#
# WHAT: one verify_ed25519 arm using ed25519_dalek (already a workspace
# dependency, used for cosignatures) + one Cargo line + an openssl-verified
# Ed25519 root/intermediate/leaf fixture chain + a test_validate_chain! case.
# Uses verify_strict (rejects non-canonical points and small-order keys),
# matching what a CT log should accept.
#
# PROOF: cargo test -p x509_util → 29 passed (28 existing + ed25519_chain_success);
# with the match arm removed, ed25519_chain_success FAILS and nothing else
# changes. cargo clippy -p x509_util -- -D warnings: clean.
#
# Generated 2026-08-28 against azul HEAD 2051772. Tracked by notme-1b46a8.
# Apply with: git apply docs/design/azul-ed25519.patch (from the azul checkout).

